  "name": "Dividing by 5, 25, and 50",
  "rule": "÷5: double it, then ÷10. ÷25: times 4, then ÷100. ÷50: double it, then ÷100.",
  "example": "240 ÷ 5 = 480 ÷ 10 = 48     300 ÷ 25 = 1200 ÷ 100 = 12",
  "why": "5 is half of 10, so dividing by 5 is the same as doubling and dividing by 10. The same idea works for 25 (a quarter of 100) and 50 (half of 100).",
